course: dictionary
lesson: 13984
title: Lofty: high, grand or proud
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The lofty mountains were covered in snow.» Lofty means very high or tall, so these mountains reach up very high into the sky.
explain: «She had lofty ambitions to become a doctor and cure diseases.» Here lofty does not mean tall. Ask what word would fit: grand or ambitious. Try ambitious in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «He spoke in a lofty manner, as if no one else was as clever as him.» Lofty can also mean proud and acting better than others. The clues are «as if» and «no one else», which tell you he thinks he is superior.
fact: Lofty means very high or tall, as in «lofty mountains».
fact: Lofty can mean grand, noble or ambitious, as in «lofty ideas» and «lofty goals».
fact: Lofty can mean proud and acting as if you are better than others, as in «a lofty manner».
fact: In Australia and the UK, «Lofty» is a jokey nickname, sometimes for a very tall person.
fact: Useful phrases: lofty ambitions, lofty heights, lofty goals.
exercise: «The lofty tower could be seen from miles away.» What does lofty mean here? | *Very high | Very quiet | Very cheap | Very sleepy
exercise: «Her lofty goals included winning a gold medal and climbing the highest peak.» What does lofty mean in «lofty goals»? | Sad and lost | *Big and ambitious | Small and easy
exercise: Priya tells her brother, «Stop acting so lofty.» What does she mean? | Stop climbing so high up the tree | Stop eating so fast | Stop singing so loudly | *Stop acting proud and as if you are better than everyone
test: «The lofty trees swayed gently in the wind.» What does lofty mean? | Very wet | Very kind | Very short | *Very tall
test: Mates in Australia call Jamie «Lofty», even though he is very tall. What does this nickname tell us? | It is his real name, given at birth | It means he is a grand king | *It is a joking nickname | It means he can fly
exam: Mrs Lee says, «Aim for lofty heights, but keep your feet on the ground.» What does lofty heights mean? | Deep caves underground | Heights of mountains you can climb | Shoes with very high heels | *Very great success and high aims
